    {
      "id": "6r377hm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Master foundational concepts and rules for converting between percentages, fractions, and decimals.",
        "Memorize important percentage values for fast mental math in competitive exams.",
        "Learn systematically to calculate percentage increase, decrease, and net successive percentage changes.",
        "Apply reverse percentage techniques to solve complex multi-step quantitative problems."
      ],
      "id": "xwd23r7"
    },
    {
      "id": "0my3hf6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Percentage means 'per hundred'.<br></br>1% = 1/100",
        "Percentage is used to express increase or decrease, comparison, profit and loss, marks, population, growth, etc.<br></br><br></br><em>In SSC examination, percentage questions are direct, formula-based, and often linked with Ratio, Profit–Loss and Simple Interest.</em>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e9jujbh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. CONVERSION RULES"
    },
    {
      "id": "rlpya28",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Fraction to Percentage:<br></br>(a/b) × 100<br></br>Example: 3/5 = 60%",
        "Percentage to Fraction:<br></br>x% = x/100<br></br>Example: 25% = 1/4",
        "Decimal to Percentage:<br></br>Multiply the decimal by 100<br></br>Example: 0.75 = 75%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05c64lu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
